Z||000000||88formula||05-07-2000||10:47 AM||||I considering putting in the stroker crankshaft and boring the cylinders .030 to make my 2.8 a 3.2 liter engine. I need lots of information on this like web sites and your commentary. I need your help guys on which pistons, rings, crank year, and so on to make this happen.<P>Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero Jon||05-07-2000||09:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>I considering putting in the stroker crankshaft and boring the cylinders .030 to make my 2.8 a 3.2 liter engine. I need lots of information on this like web sites and your commentary. I need your help guys on which pistons, rings, crank year, and so on to make this happen.<P>Thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero Jon||05-07-2000||10:06 PM||||Sorry, hit the wrong key and replied your quote, duh!  Your question depends on some things, but mainly what do you want to accomplish?  If you just want more power, go with a kit from PISA or FOCOA.  Word of warning on FOCOA--they're having problems right now and aren't getting their stuff off the shelf real quick.  PISA's kit includes the pistons, rings, crank, fuel pressure regulator, and other misc. items.  If you want a decent cam go with the 3.4 cam in the GM Performance Catalogue.  You will have to have your rods refurbished to accomodate the longer stroke.  If you don't want to use a kit--any 3.1 (or 3.4) crank will work. You still have to do the connecting rods, and you have to get more fuel to the cylinders (injectors off a 3.4 or a SBC will work).  Over sized pistons are available through Performance Automotive Warehouse (www.pawinc.com) and JCWhitney (not on the web get the catalogue.  E-mail me if you have any questions.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||05-08-2000||01:55 AM||||Silvolite 1486 pistons are for 3.1L iron head. They quote 8.8:1, but they meet the 8.9:1 specifications. Available in std and oversize.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||05-08-2000||02:25 PM||||3.1s use the same rods as the 2.8s.<BR>||||reg||1
